From 091f02a7eac3a09160c7991372efcb0212d74ed3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Schmitz <jan.schmitz@whu.edu>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 10:04:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix audit findings: RBAC hierarchy, color CSS injection, SVG
 XSS, MIME spoof, SSRF, IDOR
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-on security audit triggered by the externally reported stored XSS
that pivoted to /members/invite/. The XSS sink itself was already fixed in
prior commits; this batch closes the rest of the surface so an attacker who
ever gets a similar foothold has nowhere to escalate.

* members: enforce role-hierarchy on invite + workspace assignments +
  update_member_role — strict on org_role (only owners can grant admin),
  non-strict on workspace_role bounded by inviter's own role in that
  workspace (org owners bypass via implicit ws-owner).
* calendar: validate hex colors at view + model layers, gate
  event_create/edit/delete behind create_posts permission (viewers were
  able to create CSS-injectable shared events), scope queue_create
  category_id to the request workspace.
* media_library: drop image/svg+xml from the allow-list (script-bearing
  SVG executed same-origin on local storage) and replace
  content_type-based validation with a magic-byte sniffer so a
  spoofed-Content-Type masquerade is rejected before storage.
* composer feeds: re-validate every periodic fetch through is_safe_url +
  reject redirects to private IPs (was follow_redirects=True with no
  per-hop check, opening DNS-rebind / 302->internal).
* notifications: re-validate webhook URL at dispatch time, refuse 3xx
  redirect responses (no more 302->127.0.0.1).
* inbox/webhooks + composer feeds: route XML through safe_xml_fromstring
  (5 MB cap + DOCTYPE/ENTITY rejection) to close the billion-laughs DoS.
* approvals: scope edit_comment's Post lookup + comment query to the
  request workspace so a viewer in WS-A cannot edit/leak comments on a
  post in WS-B by guessing the UUIDs.

No new dependencies — defusedxml and python-magic both intentionally
avoided to keep the buildpack lean; the size-cap + DOCTYPE/ENTITY
prefix-scan and the hand-rolled magic-byte table cover the same threats.

Tests: +30 (325 total passing). Migrations: 3 (validator-only on
workspaces, calendar, composer color fields).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
